ption>␀␀<h2 id='␀␀␀␀</h2>␀␀␀<a href='#firmware'>Firmware</a>␀␀␀␀(saved â€” leave blank to keep)␀AIzaâ€¦␀ open␀␀␀ (saved &#10003;)␀␀␀ (needed for Twitch channels)␀␀␀ minute␀ minutes␀␀␀␀ required␀␀␀Password␀␀␀␀New PIN␀Choose a PIN (4â€“12 characters)␀␀␀␀Leave blank to keep the current PIN␀e.g. 4 digits␀␀␀<h1>&#9654; SubCounter settings</h1><p>Saved on the board only. v10.4␀␀␀ &middot; <a href='/'>&larr; Dashboard</a>␀␀</p><nav class='jump'><a href='#channels'>YouTube</a><a href='#twitch'>Twitch</a><a href='#display'>Display</a><a href='#alerts'>Alerts</a><a href='#weather'>Weather</a><a href='#spotify'>Spotify</a><a href='#motion'>Motion</a><a href='#wifi'>Wi-Fi</a><a href='#security'>Security</a>␀␀␀␀</nav>␀␀<div style='background:#3a1210;border:1px solid #e62117;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;margin-bottom:8px;font-size:14px'><b>Couldn't connect to Wi-Fi:</b><br>␀<form method='POST' action='/save'>␀<label>YouTube channels (one per line)</label>␀␀<textarea name='channels' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='@yourchannel&#10;@mkbhd&#10;@veritasium'>␀␀</textarea>␀<small>@handles, UCâ€¦ channel IDs or channel links. Put your own channel first â€“ it's highlighted and shown on the night clock.</small>␀␀<label>YouTube Data API key</label>␀<input name='apikey' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' placeholder='␀␀'><small>Only needed if you follow YouTube channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Twitch channels (just the name, one per line)</label>␀␀␀␀<textarea name='twch' autocapitalize='off' autocorrect='off' spellcheck='false' style='min-height:90px' placeholder='shroud&#10;pokimane'>␀␀<small>Type the name as it appears in their Twitch address (twitch.tv/<b>name</b>). Pasting the full link works too. YouTube and Twitch together: up to 10 channels.</small>␀␀␀␀<small style='color:#e62117'>␀␀␀<details␀␀␀␀><summary>Twitch app details␀␀␀␀<small>Create a free app at <a href='https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps' target='_blank'>dev.twitch.tv/console</a>: Register Your Application &rarr; any unique name &rarr; OAuth Redirect URL <code>https://localhost</code> (any https address works, it isn't used) &rarr; Category: Other &rarr; Client type: Confidential &rarr; Create &rarr; Manage &rarr; copy the Client ID and a <b>New Secret</b>. Your Twitch account needs two-factor sign-in turned on.</small>␀␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='twid' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' value='␀␀<label>Client Secret</label><input name='twsec' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀Display␀display␀Switch channels automatically every 10 seconds␀␀Estimated live counts between YouTube's rounded steps (â€œest.â€)␀␀<label>Show the big clock after this long without use</label><select name='idleclk'>␀␀␀␀Never␀␀␀</select><small>Touch, press BOOT or pick the board up to go back.</small>␀␀<label>Night clock (dims and shows the time)</label><div class='row'>␀␀␀nightStart␀␀<span>to</span>␀nightEnd␀␀␀␀<label>Subscriber race</label><div class='row'>␀<span>vs</span>␀<small>Swipe down twice from the main count to see it.</small>␀␀Alerts␀␀alerts␀␀Confetti for milestones (bigger milestones, bigger party)␀␀␀Alert when a channel goes live (and switch to it)␀␀␀Daily summary at 9 am (a monthly recap on the 1st)␀␀<small>New-subscriber, overtake and record alerts are always on. Alerts are skipped at night, when the board is face-down, and while Spotify is playing.</small>␀␀␀␀weather␀<label>Town or city</label><input name='wxtown' value='␀' placeholder='e.g. Glasgow'>␀␀␀<small>Long-press the board's screen and pick Weather. Forecasts from Open-Meteo.</small>␀␀␀spotify␀<p class='ok'>Connected &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀><summary>Spotify app details (one-time setup, needs Premium)</summary>␀<small>Put the relay page on GitHub Pages (or any https address you own), then at <b>developer.spotify.com/dashboard</b> &rarr; Create app &rarr; add that https address as the Redirect URI &rarr; tick <b>Web API</b> &rarr; Save. Copy the Client ID, Client secret and the same Redirect URI here, and save.</small>␀␀␀␀<label>Redirect URI (exactly as entered at Spotify)</label><input name='spredir' value='␀␀␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='https://yourname.github.io/spotify-callback/'>␀␀<label>Client ID</label><input name='spid' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off'>␀␀<label>Client secret</label><input name='spsecret' type='text' class='secret' autocapitalize='off' autocomplete='off' spellcheck='false' placeholder='␀␀<a class='btnlink' href='␀␀␀'>Connect Spotify</a><small>Press Agree on Spotify's page and you'll be brought straight back here.</small><details><summary>The relay page showed a code instead?</summary><label>Paste the code or that page's full address</label><input name='url' placeholder='code or full address' autocapitalize='off'><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/code' formnovalidate>Use this code</button></details>␀␀<button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/spotify/disconnect' formnovalidate>Disconnect Spotify</button>␀␀␀␀<small>Save the app details first; a <b>Connect Spotify</b> button then appears here.</small>␀␀␀Motion␀␀motion␀␀<small style='color:#e62117'>Motion sensor not detected.</small>␀␀␀␀Shake to refresh␀␀␀␀Face-down turns the screen off␀␀Stand it on its side for a tall leaderboard␀Tall leaderboard is upside down? Tick to flip it␀␀␀␀Double-tap the desk for the next channel␀␀␀␀<label>Desk tap sensitivity</label><select name='tapsens'>␀␀Low (firm knocks)␀␀␀Medium␀␀High (light taps)␀␀␀<label>Calibration</label><small>Put the board in the position you normally use it (on its stand or flat), then press:</small><button type='submit' class='b2' formaction='/calibrate' formnovalidate>Set this as the normal position</button>␀␀edit␀␀␀␀Wi-Fi networks␀␀wifi␀␀␀␀<small>The board joins your <b>Preferred</b> network when it's in range, otherwise the strongest saved one. <b>Connect now</b> switches straight away.</small><div class='st' style='margin:10px 0'>␀␀␀␀<label style='margin:4px 0 0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='-1' style='width:auto'␀<div class='saved'><b>␀␀</b>␀␀␀␀<span style='color:#30d158'>connected</span>␀␀␀␀<button type='submit' formaction='/wifi/connect?n=␀␀' formnovalidate class='mini'>Connect now</button>␀␀<span>fixed IP</span>␀␀␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='radio' name='pref' value='␀' style='width:auto'␀␀␀␀> Preferred</label>␀<a href='/settings?edit=␀␀␀␀#wifi'>Edit</a>␀<label style='margin:0'><input type='checkbox' name='rm␀' value='1' style='width:auto'> Remove</label></div>␀␀␀␀> No preference (strongest signal wins)</label>␀<label>␀Editing: ␀␀␀Add another network (e.g. home)␀Wi-Fi network␀␀␀<button type='button' id='scanBtn' onclick='scan()' class='b2' style='margin-top:6px'>&#128246; Scan for networks</button>␀␀<div id='nets' style='margin:8px 0'></div>␀␀<input id='s' name='ssid' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='Network name (tap one above, or type it)'␀␀␀␀<small>Leave blank if you're not adding a network.</small>␀␀<label>Wi-Fi password</label>␀␀␀<input id='pw' name='pass' type='password' autocomplete='off' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='␀␀␀␀'><small><label style='display:inline;margin:0'><input type='checkbox' style='width:auto' onclick="document.getElementById('pw').type=this.checked?'text':'password'"> Show password</label></small>␀␀␀␀<label>Username (only for work Wi-Fi that asks for one)</label>␀<input name='user' value='␀␀' autocapitalize='off' placeholder='Leave blank for normal Wi-Fi'>␀␀><summary>Advanced settings for this network</summary>␀␀Compatibility mode (Wi-Fi 4 instead of Wi-Fi 6)␀<label>Fixed IP address (blank = automatic)</label>␀<input name='ip' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.250' inputmode='decimal'>␀<label>Gateway (router) address</label>␀<input name='gw' value='␀␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 192.168.1.1' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<label>Subnet mask</label>␀␀<input name='mask' value='␀␀' placeholder='255.255.255.0' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀<label>DNS server</label>␀␀␀<input name='dns' value='␀␀␀' placeholder='e.g. 8.8.8.8' inputmode='decimal'>␀␀␀<small>If this one doesn't answer, the board also tries 8.8.8.8.</small>␀␀␀␀Security␀␀␀␀security␀␀␀␀<p class='ok'>PIN is on &#10003;</p>␀␀␀␀<small>No PIN set: anyone on your Wi-Fi can open this page and change things.</small>␀␀␀</label><input name='pin' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12' placeholder='␀␀<label>Type it again</label><input name='pin2' type='password' inputmode='numeric' autocomplete='new-password' maxlength='12'>␀␀Remove the PIN␀␀nopin␀␀␀<small>After you save, your browser asks for it whenever you open Settings or Update: user name <b>admin</b>, password = your PIN. The dashboard stays open to view. Forgotten it? Hold BOOT for 3 seconds: setup mode doesn't ask for it, so you can change it there.</small>␀␀<div class='savebar'><button type='submit'>Save &amp; restart</button></div>␀␀␀␀</form>␀Firmware␀␀␀␀firmware␀␀␀␀<p style='margin:0'>Running <b>v10.4</b> &middot; <a href='/update'>&#11014; Update wirelessly</a></p>␀␀<small style='margin-top:16px'>Board Wi-Fi MAC address: ␀␀␀␀</small></div>␀␀<script>scan()</script>␀<h1>␀␀␀␀</h1><p>␀␀␀␀</p><a href='/settings'>Go back</a></div></body></html>␀Calibrated &#10003;␀This is now the board's normal position.␀␀␀␀Unknown network␀That network isn't saved.␀␀␀Switching to ␀␀␀&hellip;␀␀␀␀The board is leaving this network now, so this page will stop updating. Join <b>␀␀␀␀</b> yourself and use the new address shown on the board's leaderboard. If it can't connect, it goes back to the best network it can find.␀␀Spotify disconnected␀␀␀␀You can connect it again any time.␀␀/settings␀␀␀/save␀␀␀/calibrate␀␀/api/data␀␀␀/api/history␀␀␀␀/api/csv␀␀␀␀/api/scan␀␀␀/wifi/connect␀␀␀/update␀/spotify/code␀␀␀/spotify/callback␀␀␀/spotify/disconnect␀, open␀␀, needs username␀␀␀␀<option value="␀">␀␀ dBm␀␀␀␀)</option>␀␀Joined Wi-Fi but got no IP address (DHCP / device approval?)␀␀␀␀Timed out with n